  "paper_id": "ccs-2024-characterizing-ethereum-address-poisoning-attack-21cda205",
  "title": "Characterizing Ethereum Address Poisoning Attack",
  "abstract": "This paper presents the first comprehensive analysis of the address poisoning attack surged on the Ethereum blockchain. This phishing attack typically exploits the address shortening feature of Ethereum explorers and digital wallets (e.g., Etherscan and MetaMask) by crafting token transfer events with a seemingly correct address to poison victims' transfer history, waiting for them to mistakenly transfer assets to the attacker's address.",
